# Agreements

The ten decisions `CONSTITUTION.md` §5 requires every team to settle and write down, and the project's adjustments to
the working agreements in §5. Each decision starts as the kit's proposed default. A row becomes an agreement when the
team fills in its choice, sets its status to `agreed`, and records the date and who decided. Settle every row before the first change reaches production. The
`settling-agreements` skill runs this as a session, and infers current practice from the repository.

A current practice that breaks the safety floor is not an agreement. Record it as a gap, with an owner and a date.

| Decision | Proposed default | Status | Choice | Date | Decider |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Branching and merge strategy | A story branch per story, one PR per phase. The author merges once checks are green. Shared branches are never force-pushed; they are updated by merging. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% if release_workflow %}
| Deployment workflow and its environments | A pre-release builds the image once and deploys it to dev. Marking the release final promotes the same digest to prod. Environments: dev and prod. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
| Rollback workflow | Traffic rolls back automatically when the post-deploy smoke checks fail. A problem found later is rolled back by dispatching the release workflow on the last good tag with `rollback=true` (`docs/runbooks/rollback.md`); anyone who can dispatch workflows can trigger it. Rehearsed once on dev before the first production release. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
| Hotfix path | A fix branch from `main` through the normal checks, then a final release that skips the pre-release and says so. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% else %}
