{% else %}
| Deployment workflow and its environments | None proposed. The release workflow was not rendered; render it with `copier update --trust --answers-file .copier-answers.praxis-kit.yml --data release_workflow=true` or settle another. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% endif %}
| Rollback workflow | None proposed until a release workflow exists. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
| Hotfix path | None proposed until a release workflow exists. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% endif %}
{% if team_delivery %}
| Review norms | Reviews are not required; checks gate the merge. The author labels a one-way change and requests a review, and each story names a second reviewer. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% else %}
| Review norms | Reviews are not required; checks gate the merge. A one-way change gets a review before it merges. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% endif %}
{% if release_workflow %}
| Definition of done | Merged with checks green, deployed to dev and verified there, and closed with actual effort and waiting time recorded. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% else %}
| Definition of done | Merged with checks green, and closed with actual effort and waiting time recorded. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% endif %}
| Versioning and release notes | Semantic version tags on GitHub releases (`v1.4.0-rc.1` as a pre-release, then final), with notes generated by GitHub (`gh release create --generate-notes`). | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% if team_delivery %}
| Incident handling | The on-call role responds first and the architecture decider is accountable (`docs/raci.md`). Alarms go to the team channel. Each production incident gets a blameless postmortem in `docs/runbooks/incidents/`. When the error budget is spent, non-critical deploys freeze and reliability work goes first, labelled `unplanned` (`docs/slo.md`). | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% else %}
| Incident handling | The project owner responds first. Alarms go to a channel the owner watches, not one inbox. Each production incident gets a blameless postmortem in `docs/runbooks/incidents/`. When the error budget is spent, non-critical deploys freeze and reliability work goes first (`docs/slo.md`). | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
{% endif %}
| Response expectations | Reviews and questions are answered within one working day. Nobody is expected to answer outside agreed working hours, except on-call during an incident. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |
| How these agreements change | A PR to this file. The named decider decides and informs; silence for three working days is consent. | proposed, not yet agreed | | | |

